    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1066">

                <pb facs="1097" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg977"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Hutchinson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-12-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 10, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 372.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 369, of the 27th
                    ultimo, having to do with the New York and Bermudez Company affair, I have the
                    honor to inclose copies of notes exchanged between this legation and the
                    ministry of foreign relations.</p>
                <p>The note of the minister is in answer to my note of November 26, which the
                    Department will find inclosed with my above-named dispatch.</p>
                <p>My note of December 2 was sent to the minister to act as an explanation of my
                    note of November 26 and at the same time to acknowledge his note of December 1,
                    above mentioned.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman
                    Hutchinson.</hi></signed></closer>



